Tom: I''d love to visit the national park to watch wild birds.
Lily: That sounds great. What do you hope to see there?
Tom: Mostly eagles. I really want to take a photo of one flying.
Lily: Then we should get up very early in the morning.
Tom: Yes, dawn is the time when most birds are active.
Lily: Good idea. I''ll bring my camera too.
Tom: Perfect. Remember to stay quiet so we don''t frighten them away.', 'Lily 问 Tom 周末想去哪;Tom 想去国家公园观野鸟,主要想拍飞翔的鹰;两人决定清晨早起,因为黎明时鸟最活跃;Lily 也带相机;Tom 提醒要保持安静,以免吓跑鸟。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Where does Tom want to go this weekend?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["To the national park.","To a shopping centre.","To the seaside.","To a friend''s house."]},{"q":"What does Tom mainly hope to see?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Wild horses.","Eagles.","Whales.","Snakes."]},{"q":"Why do they decide to get up early?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Because most birds are active at dawn.","To avoid the rain.","To buy cheap tickets.","Because the park closes at noon."]},{"q":"What will Lily bring along?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["A map.","Her camera.","Some food.","A warm coat."]},{"q":"What does Tom remind Lily to do?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Walk as fast as possible.","Sing on the way.","Stay quiet so they do not frighten the birds.","Leave the camera at home."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required1', 'U5', 'fltrp');
When food runs low in winter, they move to warmer areas.
Some travel a long way to find a safe place for their young.
Birds, fish and even some insects make these yearly journeys.
The trips are full of danger, but they help the animals live on.', '许多动物并非整年待在一个地方;冬天食物变少时,它们迁往温暖地区;有些长途跋涉为幼崽寻找安全之地;鸟、鱼甚至一些昆虫都进行这样的年度旅程;旅途充满危险,但帮助动物生存下去。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What do many animals NOT do?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Look for food.","Move in winter.","Care for their young.","Spend the whole year in one place."]},{"q":"Why do animals move when winter comes?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Food becomes hard to find.","They enjoy the cold.","They want to swim.","They are bored."]},{"q":"Why do some animals travel a long way?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["To meet people.","To find a safe place for their young.","To find shops.","To get lost."]},{"q":"Which animals make these yearly journeys?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Only large animals.","Only sea animals.","Birds, fish and even some insects.","No animals at all."]},{"q":"What do these dangerous trips help animals do?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Forget the way home.","Stop eating.","Sleep all winter.","Live on and survive."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required1', 'U5', 'fltrp');
Jack: But a zoo can never give an animal its real home in the wild.
Mia: That''s true, yet zoos help children learn about animals.
Jack: They can learn from films and books instead.
Mia: Still, seeing a real tiger is not the same as watching a film.
Jack: I agree it''s exciting, but I worry the animals are not free.
Mia: So you think zoos are built more for people than for animals?
Jack: Exactly. That''s my biggest reason for being against them.', 'Mia 认为动物园好,因为能保护濒危动物;Jack 认为动物园永远给不了动物真正的野外家园;Mia 说动物园能让孩子了解动物;Jack 说看影片和书也能学;Mia 说亲眼看真老虎和看影片不一样;Jack 担心动物不自由,认为动物园更多是为人而建——这是他反对的最大理由。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Why does Mia think zoos are good?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["They protect animals in danger.","They make a lot of money.","They are quiet places.","They are easy to build."]},{"q":"What is Jack''s first point against zoos?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Zoos are too small.","A zoo cannot give an animal its real wild home.","Zoos cost too much.","Zoos have no visitors."]},{"q":"How does Mia reply when Jack mentions films and books?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["She agrees films are best.","She says books are useless.","She says seeing a real tiger is not the same as a film.","She stops talking."]},{"q":"What does Jack worry about?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["The price of tickets.","The weather in the zoo.","The food for visitors.","That the animals are not free."]},{"q":"What is Jack''s biggest reason for being against zoos?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["He believes zoos are built more for people than for animals.","He dislikes children.","He thinks animals are boring.","He never visits zoos."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required1', 'U5', 'fltrp');
For years, no one knew how they found the right way.
Scientists learned that the insect uses the sun to guide it.
Sadly, the number of monarchs has dropped very fast.
People are now working together to help them survive.', '每年秋天,黑脉金斑蝶向南飞行数千公里;多年来无人知道它们如何找到正确方向;科学家发现这种昆虫靠太阳指引;遗憾的是,金斑蝶数量下降得很快;如今人们正合力帮助它们生存。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"When do the monarch butterflies fly south?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Every morning.","Each autumn.","In summer only.","Once in their life."]},{"q":"What did people NOT know for years?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["What the butterflies ate.","Where the butterflies slept.","How the butterflies found the right way.","How big the butterflies were."]},{"q":"What guides the butterfly, according to scientists?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["The wind.","Other birds.","The rivers.","The sun."]},{"q":"What has happened to the number of monarchs?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["It has dropped very fast.","It has stayed the same.","It has grown quickly.","It is unknown."]},{"q":"What are people doing now?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Catching all of them.","Working together to help them survive.","Ignoring the problem.","Moving them to zoos."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required1', 'U5', 'fltrp');
Sara: Yes. Never get too close to a wild bear.
Ben: How close is too close?
Sara: Keep at least a hundred metres away to stay safe.
Ben: What if a bear suddenly looks at me?
Sara: Stay calm, don''t run, and move back slowly.
Ben: That''s good to know. Anything else?
Sara: Yes, always respect the animal. We are visitors in its world.', 'Ben 下周要拍熊,向 Sara 求建议;Sara 说绝不要太靠近野熊,至少保持一百米;若熊忽然看着你,要保持冷静、别跑、慢慢后退;最后她说要永远尊重动物,我们是它世界里的客人。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is Ben going to do next week?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Sell his camera.","Visit a city.","Photograph bears.","Stay at home."]},{"q":"What is Sara''s first piece of advice?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Feed the bears.","Shout at the bears.","Touch the bears.","Never get too close to a wild bear."]},{"q":"How far away should Ben stay to be safe?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["At least a hundred metres.","About one metre.","About ten metres.","As close as possible."]},{"q":"What should Ben do if a bear looks at him?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Run away fast.","Stay calm and move back slowly.","Throw something.","Climb a tree."]},{"q":"What does Sara say at the end?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Bears are not real.","Cameras are useless.","Always respect the animal.","Bears love people."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'required1', 'U5', 'fltrp');
When we visit their world, we should be quiet and careful.
We must never leave rubbish that could harm them.
Cutting down their forests takes away the homes they need.
If we respect them, both animals and people can live well.', '野生动物不是宠物,它们属于大自然;当我们进入它们的世界时,应保持安静和小心;绝不能留下可能伤害它们的垃圾;砍伐森林会夺走它们所需的家园;如果我们尊重它们,动物和人都能生活得很好。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does the passage say about wild animals?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["They make good pets.","They like living in cities.","They are all dangerous.","They are not pets and belong in nature."]},{"q":"How should we behave when visiting their world?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Quietly and carefully.","Loudly and freely.","Quickly and carelessly.","Angrily and rudely."]},{"q":"What must we never leave behind?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Our cameras.","Rubbish that could harm them.","Our footprints.","Our maps."]},{"q":"What does cutting down forests do?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["It helps the animals.","It makes them happy.","It takes away the homes they need.","It gives them more food."]},{"q":"What happens if we respect wild animals?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only people benefit.","Animals disappear faster.","Nothing changes at all.","Both animals and people can live well."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'required1', 'U5', 'fltrp');

